# INNOGRIT IG5236 "RainierPC" NVMe controllers (HP SSD FX900 Pro, Adata Legend
# 850, and other rebadges) mishandle PCIe power-state transitions.
#
# 20-nvme-apst.sh already disables NVMe APST via
# nvme_core.default_ps_max_latency_us=0, which stops the *idle* dropouts:
#   nvme nvmeN: controller is down; will reset: CSTS=0xffffffff, PCI_STATUS=0x10
#
# That karg does not cover suspend/resume. On S3, pm_suspend_via_firmware() is
# true, so nvme_suspend() takes the full-shutdown branch and nvme_resume() does a
# complete controller reset — meaning every resume is an NVMe re-init plus a PCIe
# link retrain out of D3. This controller does not reliably survive that. Measured
# on fury4dx (4 TB FX900 Pro holding the whole OS): 2 of 4 suspends never resumed,
# a 3rd resumed only after a controller reset, and the upstream port logged PCIe
# correctable RxErr / Data Link Layer Timeout storms. When the drive holds root,
# a resume that does not recover takes the filesystem read-only.
#
# Disabling ASPM L1 — including the PCI-PM L1 substates, which are the ones that
# engage when the device is put into D3hot for suspend — removes the link
# power-state transitions from that path. Blocking d3cold keeps the controller
# from losing main power across the cycle.
#
# Side benefit: with ASPM off, pcie_aspm_enabled() returns false, which forces
# nvme_suspend() down the full-shutdown branch even under s2idle. Without that,
# s2idle would instead park the drive in its deepest non-operational power state
# (PS4 on this device: 0.008 W, 85 ms exit latency) — the exact state that hangs
# it. So this also makes s2idle safe, not just deep.
#
# Gated on the controller PCI ID so machines without this silicon keep their PCIe
# power savings. Substates are cleared before the l1_aspm master knob so the
# teardown order is well defined. Verified on fury4dx: writing l1_aspm=0 leaves
# lspci reporting "ASPM Disabled" with all four L1 substates cleared.
ACTION=="add|bind", SUBSYSTEM=="pci", ATTR{vendor}=="0x1dbe", ATTR{device}=="0x5236", \
    ATTR{link/l1_2_pcipm}="0", ATTR{link/l1_1_pcipm}="0", \
    ATTR{link/l1_2_aspm}="0", ATTR{link/l1_1_aspm}="0", \
    ATTR{link/l1_aspm}="0", ATTR{d3cold_allowed}="0"
